Subject: [PATCH] Validate and migrate OpenSolo saved timestamp formats

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenSolo legacy 12-digit timestamp migration]

The old controller checkpoint service wrote minute-resolution values.
Validate the numeric format and convert those values before the modern
bootmisc seconds-resolution comparison.

--- a/bootmisc.sh
+++ b/bootmisc.sh
@@ -75,6 +75,12 @@
 then
 	SYSTEMDATE=`date -u +%4Y%2m%2d%2H%2M%2S`
 	read TIMESTAMP < "$TIMESTAMP_FILE"
+    case "$TIMESTAMP" in
+        *[!0-9]*|'') TIMESTAMP=0 ;;
+        ????????????) TIMESTAMP="${TIMESTAMP}00" ;;
+        ??????????????) ;;
+        *) TIMESTAMP=0 ;;
+    esac
 	if [ ${TIMESTAMP} -gt $SYSTEMDATE ]; then
 		# format the timestamp as date expects it (2m2d2H2M4Y.2S)
 		TS_YR=${TIMESTAMP%??????????}
